From: Reframed VR contributors
Subject: [PATCH] tty: preserve bare earlycon handling with Pico console switch

The early-parameter parser passes NULL for a bare earlycon option. Pico's
console-off extension dereferences it before the existing device-tree/SPCR
fallback, panicking during setup_arch. Keep the off option while allowing the
upstream fallback to handle a missing parameter.

--- a/drivers/tty/serial/earlycon.c
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/earlycon.c
@@ -215,7 +215,7 @@ static int __init param_setup_earlycon(char *buf)
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_SERIAL_CORE_CONSOLE
 	pr_err("%s(): serial console/earlycon %s\n", __func__, buf);
-	if(*buf) {
+	if (buf && *buf) {
 		if(!strcmp("off", buf)){
 			do_skip_serial = 1;
 			pr_err("%s: do_skip_serial = %d\n", __func__, do_skip_serial);
